// REJECTS: Field 'mapping' is required
//
// An execution context that names a `defaultRuntime` but no `mapping`. The .g4 gives no hint
// of this: dataSpaceExecutionContext is a `( ... )*` alternation in which every field is
// optional and order-free, so the tree builds cleanly. DataSpaceParseTreeWalker enforces the
// real rule afterwards -- a context must define EXACTLY ONE of `mapping` / `mappingProvider`,
// throwing at :206 when neither is present and at :210 when both are.
//
// This is the shape of divergence a rewrite falls into by default: transcribe the grammar,
// get a permissive parser, and discover the constraint only when a downstream compiler
// dereferences a null mapping. `name` and `defaultRuntime` are supplied so the failure can
// only be about the mapping.
###DataSpace
DataSpace fixture::neg::ContextWithoutMapping
{
  executionContexts:
  [
    {
      name: 'Context 1';
      defaultRuntime: fixture::neg::Runtime;
    }
  ];
  defaultExecutionContext: 'Context 1';
}
